{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Make yourself an ark of gopher wood.</b> Gopher is a wood called קדרו\"ס and it is light upon the face of the waters; Onkelos translated אעין דקדרוס, and it is a species of cedar. And the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded Noah to make himself an ark from this known wood and to bring into it from every species of living creature — from clean beasts and clean birds, seven, for the purpose of sacrifice; and from the unclean beasts and unclean birds, two of each, male and female, so that the species might be preserved. He informed him that He, blessed be He, is destined to bring a flood upon the world to destroy all flesh in which is the breath of life." "<b>And here</b> the discerning reader asks: since Noah was a righteous and wholehearted man, as Scripture testified of him, and he found favor in the eyes of השם, why did he not pray on behalf of the people of his generation and turn them back to the good — as we find with our father Abraham, who immediately when the Holy One, blessed be He, informed him of the punishment of Sodom, though they were outright wicked, prayed on their behalf several times that they not be destroyed — as he said (Genesis 18:31): ״הנה נא הואלתי לדבר אל אדני״, and he further said: ״אל נא יחר לאדני״. Such was the way of the early ones and the prophets, that they would draw near to HaShem to pray before Him on behalf of the people of their generation; and so it is fitting for every leader of a generation to pray on behalf of the generation. And the answer to the matter is that the reason the righteous man refrained from praying on their behalf was not out of rebellion or treachery, but because he knew that the continued existence of the world depends on ten, as the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: the world was created with ten utterances. Had there been ten righteous men among the people of the generation, the flood would not have been brought upon them, for the world would have endured on their account. But those who came into the ark were only eight — Noah and his wife and his three sons and his three sons' wives; and since they did not reach ten, they were not worthy that the generation be saved on their account, and it was enough that Noah, who was the tenth, should save his own life and the lives of his household. And this is what you find in the prayer of Abraham: once he mentioned ten and said, ״I will not destroy for the sake of the ten,״ immediately it says ״וילך ה׳״ — because it was revealed and known before Him that there were not ten there; and Abraham was not permitted to plead in his prayer to ask before Him on behalf of the people of the generation for fewer than ten, and therefore they perished from the world. And it is the very same matter with Noah, that he was not permitted to pray on their behalf since there were not ten there. And furthermore, that here He gave them a long time to return in repentance — and they are 120 years; and blessed be the name of the Merciful One, who does not punish unless He first warns."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:52.155592319Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}